From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 12:09:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ui): retain native death text source

Retain the translated DeathInfo source before conversion to Java text
components. The acquired gameplay formatter needs original code spelling
and boundaries: it preserves internal boundary spaces, ignores bold and
italic codes, masks UTF-16 units for obfuscation and assigns opaque
palette-colored shadows. Java style projection cannot retain this input.

Send a bounded, versioned raw-text payload before the matching ordinary
Java death message when the client registers both the new channel and
native actor state. Bind it to the local actor lifetime and include the
plain Java projection for association. Existing clients and oversized
sources keep the ordinary Java path. The visibility rule hides both
native fields while retaining the cached source for a later rule change.

The original 1.26.60.5 gameplay component selects FormattingCodes for the
death-info node. Executions of its unchanged formatter establish the
listed transformations, including literal uppercase/unknown codes.
Script SHA-256:
9e7efe423b6cc8a1c1fa92756bd181675cffa51a4728bce386b0081cad1bb979.
This is a negotiated translation bridge, not a new Bedrock wire packet.

Packet regressions retain exact codes and whitespace, decode the payload
and Java projection in order, cover visibility restoration and channel
removal, and preserve the Java projection without actor negotiation or
for an oversized source. Complete native client policy, layout, input
and visual parity remain separate work.
